summary_text:
No stat in libcfile. Could use stat directly.

Need maybe include `sys/stat.h` in `libvmdk_handle.c` conditional. Time accuracy seconds. API uint64_t seconds since epoch, 0 unavailable? We can use `time_t`. On Windows st_mtime. Fine. Add helper.

But maybe more elegant create `libvmdk_snapshot.c` object. Let's design concrete implementation relative current handle fields.

Fields add:
```
	libcdata_array_t *snapshots_array;
	int active_snapshot_index;
```
Snapshot struct in new files:
```
typedef struct libvmdk_snapshot {
 system_character_t *filename;
 size_t filename_size;
 uint64_t modification_time;
 uint32_t content_identifier;
 uint32_t parent_content_identifier;
 uint8_t parent_content_identifier_set;
 uint8_t disk_type; size64_t media_size;
} libvmdk_snapshot_t;
```
We need maintain snapshot objects even after chain handles closed. Main handle's snapshot array only. Parent handles each can have snapshots? Set only on top-level? Fine. But when `free`, array free. Need parent_handle free currently checks? Inspect free.

